# Extract — Patterns — <system-name>

<!--
Phase 4 output of system-dissector. Design patterns observed in the
system that are worth porting — NOT whole components, just the ideas
and the canonical implementation. Companion to extract-components.md
(whole units) and extract-algorithms.md (computational kernels).

Filling convention:
- One pattern per section. Aim for 8-12 patterns. Fewer is acceptable
  if quality justifies it.
- Each pattern MUST cite real file:line for the canonical example.
- "How to apply" section makes the pattern actionable in a different
  codebase.
-->

## Evidence

<!--
Mandatory anti-hallucination gate. "Canonical code" snippets get copy-pasted
into other codebases — wrong snippets spread bugs. Each MUST be verified.
-->

- **Overall status**: `verified` | `estimated` | `mixed` *(pick one)*
- **Source repo**: `<path or URL>` — `<sha or tag>` [verified|estimated]
- **Pattern discovery method**: `<e.g. manual review, code-search heuristics>` [verified|estimated]
- **Maturity probe**: `<e.g. git log --follow <file>, git blame>` [verified|estimated]

### Evidence rules

- Canonical code blocks in `### 2.x` MUST be copied verbatim from the cited `file:line`.
- "Where used" references MUST be confirmed via grep — no invented call sites.
- Variation entries in `### 2.x` MUST each cite a distinct file (no duplicates).
- If 0% of pattern references are tagged, the catalog is editorial — re-verify against source.

## Como usar este documento

- **Audience**: arquiteto procurando inspiração para resolver problema X em código próprio.
- **Next action**: usar `## 1. Pattern summary` como índice, mergulhar em `## 2` no padrão escolhido.
- **Quando re-verificar**: quando novo padrão emergir no sistema alvo, ou quando variação取代 o canonical.

